    ("A table shows Sales of 4 products (P1=120, P2=180, P3=90, P4=210). What percentage of total sales is contributed by P2?", "30%. Total sales = 120 + 180 + 90 + 210 = 600. P2 share = (180 / 600) * 100 = 30%.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What percentage is P4?"),
    ("In a company of 500 employees, a pie chart shows: Engineering 40%, Sales 25%, Marketing 15%, HR 10%, Support 10%. How many employees work in Engineering and Sales combined?", "325 employees. Combined percentage = 40% + 25% = 65%. Total = 65% of 500 = 0.65 * 500 = 325 employees.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "How many degrees in the pie chart represent Engineering?"),
    ("How many degrees of a circle represent a 40% slice in a pie chart?", "144 degrees. A full circle has 360 degrees. 40% of 360 = 0.40 * 360 = 144 degrees. Formula: (Percentage / 100) * 360.", "Easy", "Concept", "", "What angle represents 25%?"),
    ("A bar chart shows Revenue over 3 years: Year 1 = $200k, Year 2 = $260k, Year 3 = $325k. What is the percentage growth from Year 1 to Year 2?", "30%. Growth = (260 - 200) / 200 * 100 = 60 / 200 * 100 = 30%.", "Easy", "Problem Solving", "", "What was growth from Year 2 to Year 3?"),
